.TH GET_COW_STATS 2 "January 2026" "TestUnix Kernel" "System Calls"
.SH NAME
get_cow_stats \- retrieve Copy-on-Write statistics
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <sys/pmap.h>
.LP
.BI "int get_cow_stats(struct pmap_stats *" stats );
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B get_cow_stats
() retrieves the current system-wide Copy-on-Write (COW) statistics from the kernel.
.PP
The
.I stats
argument points to a
.I struct pmap_stats
buffer that will be filled with the statistical data. The structure is defined as:
.PP
.ne 8
.nf
struct pmap_stats {
    uint32_t resident_count;      /* Total resident pages */
    uint32_t wired_count;         /* Wired (unpageable) pages */
    uint32_t faults;              /* Total page faults */
    uint32_t cow_faults;          /* Faults handled via COW */
    uint32_t zero_fills;          /* Zero-filled pages */
    uint32_t protection_upgrades; /* R/O -> R/W upgrades */
    uint32_t protection_downgrades; /* R/W -> R/O downgrades */
    uint32_t cow_pages_mapped;    /* Total pages currently shared via COW */
};
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, zero is returned. On error, -1 is returned, and
.I errno
is set appropriately.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EFAULT
.I stats
points to an invalid address.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pmap (9)
